  <h3>Pass 3 — 7 items. Working method</h3>

  <table class="catalog">
    <tr><td>21</td><td><span class="kind">PROCESS</span> Never ran the end-to-end suite at session start, so no baseline existed. Hours then went into proving a pre-existing failure was not caused by the change. The largest avoidable cost of the session.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>22</td><td><span class="kind">PROCESS</span> Never asked whether to timebox the crash investigation, which consumed most of a session whose goal was shipping features.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>23</td><td><span class="kind">COST</span> Announced each batch of container runs but never the running total: roughly thirty full matrix runs plus a four-gigabyte image re-pull across fourteen hours.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>24</td><td><span class="kind">PROCESS</span> Invoked the debugging discipline only after four rounds of guessing, and never invoked the completion-verification discipline at all.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>25</td><td><span class="kind">PROCESS</span> Put three unrelated concerns into one commit and never flagged the bundling. That commit is pushed.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>26</td><td><span class="kind">PROCESS</span> Shipped two features having never executed either in a browser.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>27</td><td><span class="kind">PROCESS</span> Designed a feature knowing its primary path cannot be driven by the test harness, and neither flagged nor recorded that gap.</td></tr>
  </table>

